  "result": "Perfect! All 202 tests pass, including 23 new tests for the statements feature. Here's what I added:\n\n**`src/statements.js`** (new file)\n- `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function that returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })`:\n  - **customerId**: normalized customer ID\n  - **invoices**: array of customer's invoices with:\n    - status is `'issued'` or `'partially_paid'` \n    - issueDate is on or before asOf\n    - Each with: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n    - Sorted by issueDate ascending\n  - **totalDue**: sum of all due amounts\n  - Returns `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` for unknown customers\n\n**`test/statements.test.js`** (new file)\n- 23 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Basic statement generation\n  - Customer filtering and normalization\n  - Status filtering (issued, partially_paid, excludes draft and paid)\n  - Date boundary handling\n  - Invoice sorting by issueDate\n  - Total and due calculations\n  - Interaction with payments, discounts, and vouchers\n  - Edge cases (empty invoices, multiple customers)\n\nThe statements feature integrates seamlessly with existing functionality, properly accounting for payments (via `balanceDue`), discounts, VAT, and vouchers when calculating amounts due.",
